WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.300
♪♪

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.567
-Someone said a very nice
thing to me recently.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:10.434
They say that whenever they hear
the word "corrections,"

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.300
the first thing they think
about is this segment.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:18.234
You know who said that?
Jonathan Franzen.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:21.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:31.567
[ Soft music plays ]

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:35.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:42.234
Brian Lodato
won the Thanksgiving

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:46.367
Corrections pool where the money
goes to whoever

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:50.567
has the box that lines up
with the minutes and seconds.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:54.901
I've been told by not just him
but other members of the crew

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.367
Kenny really needs this one.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:01:00.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.501
The San Diego Zoo no longer
has giant pandas.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:13.100
They have red pandas now.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.234
Do you know how you go
from giant pandas to red pandas?

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.267
Ozempic.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.701
♪♪

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.567
We do a segment called
"Surprise Inspection."

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:36.934
I read bad jokes
our writers have written.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:39.734
And then I show their picture
to shame them.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.534
Well, I was gobsmacked...

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.133
...this week when I called
for Matt Goldich's picture,

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.100
expecting this.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.567
The established Matt Goldich
surprise inspection photo

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.400
and instead
was greeted with this.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:03.033
It doesn't work with this.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:04.834
This.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:07.434
This guy writes jokes
like "Pepsi has announced

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.567
it will no longer
offer Sierra Mist soda.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.033
Oh, no. Then how will I make

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:14.734
my famous Sierra Mist stew
[tiramisu]?"

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.267
This guy writes that.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.667
This guy writes
grunge rock anthems.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.901
Pull a surprise inspection
on this guy,

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.634
he flicks a lit cigarette
in your face.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.434
And since when

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:37.834
are our writers allowed
to update their own headshots?

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:40.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:43.334
Since when?

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:44.767
I blame Lloyd.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.968
Our photographer.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.234
The next time he asks,
Lloyd, I invite you to say,

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:55.434
[Scottish accent]
"I cannae do it!"

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:59.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.434
I don't have the authority,
wee Matt!

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:07.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:18.267
[ Normal voice ] They don't fill
them that high at bars.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.701
Also in "Surprise Inspection,"

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:28.033
Bryan Donaldson had a joke
about chlamydia.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:30.434
The joke was "the FDA last week
authorized the first

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.701
at-home STD test for chlamydia.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.300
So give the FDA
a big round of clap."

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.334
Many of you pointed out clap
is slang for gonorrhea,

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.167
and Bryan wanted me to tell you
he definitely knows that.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:47.801
He can't go into why,
but he knows that.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.234
[ Two notes play ]

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.400
Chlamydia got its name from
the Greek word chlamydia,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.100
which means "cloak."

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:05.133
I mean, honest. What would be
a bigger red flag on a date?

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.000
If they had chlamydia
or if they showed up

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.467
to the restaurant in a cloak?

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.367
I'm happy to announce.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.968
Think you've noticed,
but I'll announce it anyway.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:20.734
"Closer Look" videos are once
again available in Canada

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:23.267
and to our Canadian viewers.

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:25.968
I'd just like to say
I hope you learned your lesson.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:31.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.000
You know what you did.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.968
I'm so glad
we got this cleared up.

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:40.067
The comments about this.
You know,

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:45.701
despite their reputation
for politeness,

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:49.133
Canadian people have been
so snippy about this.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:53.167
Like it was a personal choice
that I made.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.167
Somebody said,
"Oh, now you won't

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:59.367
show us 'Closer Looks,'
you jerk?"

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.901
Like this was up to me.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:05.000
Like once a week
NBC comes in and checks

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.634
which countries I'm okay

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:13.000
with the "Closer Looks"
being available to watch.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.267
Like somebody
walked in and said,

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.367
"Are you still good with
Canada?" And I'm like, "No."

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:22.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:26.901
"I've tired of Canada.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.601
Remove it.

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.901
Let them watch Kimmel."

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:46.000
I did an impression
of Werner Herzog as Shaggy

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.033
singing the lyrics
to the infidelity classic

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.133
"It Wasn't Me."

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:52.701
Many of you

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:56.934
Pointed out that I was not doing
Shaggy's lines from that song.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:06:00.801
I was doing the lines
from the other half of that song

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:03.934
that were sung by Rik Rok.

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:07.667
Shaggy's role in the song
is giver of advice.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.767
The core of that advice
you could

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:13.133
boil down to say "it wasn't me."

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:15.267
Rik Rok -- If you watched the
video, which I highly recommend,

00:06:15.267 --> 00:06:20.167
Rik Rok goes to his home
to receive this advice.

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.267
I do want to apologize
for the Rik Rok

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:27.534
erasure, though,
in the bit that I did last week.

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:30.234
He's great in the song.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:33.734
You know who I always get
Rik Rok confused with?

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:34.834
Rick...

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:39.934
♪♪

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:46.467
I love Shaggy, but Rik Rok

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:49.434
does most of the work
in that song.

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:50.834
It's funny that Shaggy
called him up and said,

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:52.601
"I've got a great song."

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:55.901
You guys remember
how Shaggy talks, right?

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:58.300
So just imagine him
talking like that while I talk.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:01.968
"Hey, Rik Rok, got
a great new song I want you on."

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:03.300
"Cool. What's it about?"
"It's about a dude

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.267
who def gets cheating --

00:07:05.267 --> 00:07:07.400
gets caught cheating because
he's dumb as a box of rocks."

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.400
"Okay, cool. And what do I do?"

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.167
"No, that's you, Rik Rok.

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:13.501
I'm gonna be in the video.
I'm going to be wearing

00:07:13.501 --> 00:07:16.467
the most kickass purple suit."

00:07:16.467 --> 00:07:18.200
Rik Rok was like, "Oh,
do I get to wear a purple suit?"

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.834
He's like, "Red turtleneck."

00:07:19.834 --> 00:07:21.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.334 --> 00:07:30.334
♪♪

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:33.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.734
This was sent to me.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:37.300
I want to establish.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:40.901
It was not a prop I asked
Ellen for.

00:07:40.901 --> 00:07:42.667
This came in the mail.

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:49.868
This is one is awkward.

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:52.934
Many of you included
the timestamp.

00:07:52.934 --> 00:07:54.300
So I became concerned

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.767
because everybody had
the same timestamp,

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:59.100
accused me of passing gas
in last week's "Correction"...

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.234
...and then tried to get away
with it like nothing happened.

00:08:03.234 --> 00:08:06.067
I went back and listened.
It's the chair.

00:08:06.067 --> 00:08:08.901
It is 100%
the sound of the chair.

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:10.200
And like, ha ha, I get it.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.534
Flatulence is funny,
but false accusations are not.

00:08:13.534 --> 00:08:16.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.267
I'm going to prove it.
I'm going to play it.

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:20.033
So listen.
And by the way, really listen

00:08:20.033 --> 00:08:22.334
because you can even
barely hear it.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:23.601
Roll it, Alex.

00:08:23.601 --> 00:08:26.133
It's Thanksgiving,
not April Fool's, Baze.

00:08:28.133 --> 00:08:29.734
[ Loud fart sound ]

00:08:29.734 --> 00:08:32.334
Um...

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:35.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.334 --> 00:08:36.734
It was lowbrow.

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:39.968
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.968 --> 00:08:43.067
It's a lowbrow joke,
but I feel like, you know,

00:08:43.067 --> 00:08:45.901
I feel like I earned it
with that Franzen ref.

00:08:45.901 --> 00:08:48.234
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:52.567
♪♪

00:08:52.567 --> 00:08:57.634
Here are some comments
from this week.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.734
I like

00:09:02.734 --> 00:09:05.734
to isolate certain comments
that really stick with me.

00:09:05.734 --> 00:09:08.133
"Hey, Seth, I never really
enjoyed you

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:09.968
on 'SNL' or anything, really."

00:09:09.968 --> 00:09:13.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:13.801 --> 00:09:15.000
"But for some reason,

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:19.334
'Closer Look'
and 'Corrections' work on me."

00:09:19.334 --> 00:09:21.000
You know, right next
to impressions camp,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.267
they have a compliment camp.

00:09:22.267 --> 00:09:25.434
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:26.868
Check it out next summer.

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:32.434
My family was on
the Thanksgiving show.

00:09:32.434 --> 00:09:35.701
Delight.
Best I feel they ever did.

00:09:35.701 --> 00:09:37.767
Loved it.
It was nice.

00:09:37.767 --> 00:09:40.300
It's nice to read comments
when people at home

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.267
also enjoy them
as much as I did.

00:09:43.267 --> 00:09:46.100
Here's one.
"Seth's brother is so good.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.033
It's like if Seth was funny
and had charisma."

00:09:49.033 --> 00:09:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:59.534
But comment of the week.
This is 88, by the way.

00:09:59.534 --> 00:10:04.534
Last week, 87th episode
of "Corrections."

00:10:04.534 --> 00:10:07.100
"I've watched all of these
and it still doesn't work."

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:16.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.934
Talked about my kids
and their middle names.

00:10:24.934 --> 00:10:28.667
My oldest's first and
middle name are Ashe Olson.

00:10:28.667 --> 00:10:31.567
Ashe Olson.

00:10:31.567 --> 00:10:34.300
Not, as one of you said, [bleep]

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:44.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.033
We'll say this.
Hard to unhear it.

00:10:46.033 --> 00:10:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:51.234 --> 00:10:53.300
"Bad news, honey.
The jackals noticed

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.734
something about Ashe's name."

00:10:55.734 --> 00:10:57.434
"Who are the jackals?"

00:10:57.434 --> 00:11:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.868 --> 00:11:03.901
"You know, from Emmy-nominated
'Corrections.'"

00:11:06.601 --> 00:11:10.234
[ Laughter ]

00:11:10.234 --> 00:11:11.767
"Honey, I can hear you
blinking."

00:11:11.767 --> 00:11:13.534
[ Laughter ]

00:11:17.067 --> 00:11:20.734
I also -- We had a great, uh,

00:11:20.734 --> 00:11:22.434
great Thanksgiving show,
and then right after it...

00:11:24.868 --> 00:11:27.634
...recorded a Thanksgiving
"Corrections."

00:11:27.634 --> 00:11:28.934
It was really a good one.

00:11:31.033 --> 00:11:32.300
I think a lot of you agreed.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:34.367
Someone even wrote "the crew
must be extra drunk

00:11:34.367 --> 00:11:35.934
because they're really
laughing this week."

00:11:35.934 --> 00:11:37.234
Or was it funny?

00:11:37.234 --> 00:11:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:46.601
I do do this for a living,
you know?

00:11:46.601 --> 00:11:50.267
Doesn't have to be
a chemical reason it played.

00:11:50.267 --> 00:11:52.767
I do a lot of work
on "Corrections."

00:11:52.767 --> 00:11:54.501
You know what
the hardest part is?

00:11:54.501 --> 00:11:58.133
Loading the comments.

00:11:58.133 --> 00:12:01.267
Believe it or not,
that's the hardest part.

00:12:01.267 --> 00:12:04.767
Sometimes these things
have like 3,000 comments.

00:12:04.767 --> 00:12:07.234
You just gotta, like,
keep scrolling down.

00:12:09.133 --> 00:12:10.367
[ Sighs ]

00:12:12.167 --> 00:12:13.767
Someone said that
they could tell

00:12:13.767 --> 00:12:16.367
the can of Slice I used
last week wasn't full.

00:12:16.367 --> 00:12:17.434
No [bleep]

00:12:17.434 --> 00:12:20.300
[ Laughter ]

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:24.601
Think I'm gonna let someone
ship me a full can of Slice,

00:12:24.601 --> 00:12:28.601
a soda
they discontinued in 2005.

00:12:28.601 --> 00:12:31.033
You think that's safe?
Yeah.

00:12:31.033 --> 00:12:33.734
I'll take a full can of Slice,
some nitro, and some glycerin.

00:12:33.734 --> 00:12:35.334
Same box.

00:12:42.667 --> 00:12:48.000
♪♪

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:51.968
Also, you know what?

00:12:51.968 --> 00:12:56.334
I was told I purse my lips weird
before taking sips of my drink.

00:12:56.334 --> 00:13:01.234
[ Laughter ]

00:13:01.234 --> 00:13:05.000
Is -- It's normal.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.200
Watch this, Shoemaker.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.567
Tell me if it's not normal.
Alex?

00:13:08.567 --> 00:13:09.701
[ Loud fart sound ]

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.167
See me next two weeks.

00:13:13.167 --> 00:13:18.167
[ Laughter ]

00:13:20.367 --> 00:13:21.701
[ Two notes play ]

00:13:31.601 --> 00:13:35.767
Scooby-Doo is not an Anunnaki
as I said.

00:13:35.767 --> 00:13:38.701
He's a descendant
of an Anunnaki

00:13:38.701 --> 00:13:41.901
like all talking animals
in that universe.

00:13:41.901 --> 00:13:45.968
That was one of 50 comments
clarifying this.

00:13:45.968 --> 00:13:47.400
Here's another one.
"Point of order --

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:50.601
Scooby is descended from a dog
who was possessed by a Anunnaki,

00:13:50.601 --> 00:13:53.400
not a descendant
from an actual Anunnaki.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.767
Through whatever
magical process,

00:13:54.767 --> 00:13:57.767
the original dog's
physiological -- physiological,"

00:13:57.767 --> 00:13:59.634
excuse me -- "attributes
were permanently changed,

00:13:59.634 --> 00:14:01.601
and those traits
continued down its lineage.

00:14:01.601 --> 00:14:05.167
The Scooby-Doo Anunnaki plot was
part of 'Mystery Incorporated,'

00:14:05.167 --> 00:14:07.501
which is one of the most popular
and well-liked Scooby series."

00:14:07.501 --> 00:14:11.234
I was also told Scooby-Doo

00:14:11.234 --> 00:14:15.634
says "ruh-roh," but the Anunnaki
pronounces it differently.

00:14:15.634 --> 00:14:17.300
Let's take a look.

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:19.067
-Oh! Rickroll.

00:14:19.067 --> 00:14:24.567
♪♪

00:14:24.567 --> 00:14:29.634
[ Laughter ]

00:14:32.667 --> 00:14:34.701
Misplayed my closer.

00:14:42.267 --> 00:14:45.067
Almost out of time.

00:14:45.067 --> 00:14:48.801
Crew eagerly
checking their watches.

00:14:48.801 --> 00:14:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:14:53.334 --> 00:14:58.067
♪♪

00:14:58.067 --> 00:15:01.400
Will this be?

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:06.534
Will this be the week
for a certain someone?

00:15:06.534 --> 00:15:10.567
♪♪

00:15:10.567 --> 00:15:14.367
Again, want to stress something.

00:15:14.367 --> 00:15:15.367
Didn't make this.

00:15:15.367 --> 00:15:18.767
[ Laughter ]

00:15:18.767 --> 00:15:21.400
Just came to the P.O. box.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.467
P.O. box.

00:15:23.801 --> 00:15:26.767
Kind of wish I hadn't looked.

00:15:26.767 --> 00:15:28.834
I did though.

00:15:28.834 --> 00:15:29.934
Couldn't believe it.

00:15:32.367 --> 00:15:35.334
[ Laughter ]

00:15:35.334 --> 00:15:45.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:45.167 --> 00:15:49.133
[ Laughter continues ]

00:15:49.133 --> 00:15:52.067
You know, every now
and then I remember

00:15:52.067 --> 00:15:53.767
why I keep you jackals around.

00:15:53.767 --> 00:15:55.367
[ Laughter ]

00:15:55.367 --> 00:15:56.801
See me next week.

